18
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:49,380
Again, people look to your face for the context

19
00:00:49,380 --> 00:00:50,719
behind what we're saying.

20
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:54,100
And if you keep a blank face, then you're not

21
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:56,000
being an effective communicator either.

22
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:57,960
I mean, again, imagine you walked in the funeral

23
00:00:57,960 --> 00:01:00,799
and you said, I'm so sorry for your loss.

24
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:04,159
They're going to still think you killed the person.

25
00:01:04,319 --> 00:01:06,079
So again, it's so important for us

26
00:01:06,079 --> 00:01:08,180
to be aware that if people are looking

27
00:01:08,180 --> 00:01:10,219
to our face for the context behind what we're saying,

28
00:01:10,379 --> 00:01:14,659
we can add further context by using our facial expressions

29
00:01:14,659 --> 00:01:15,019
more.

30
00:01:15,219 --> 00:01:17,859
And if you don't use any facial expressions at all,

31
00:01:17,959 --> 00:01:20,219
you're losing out on a world of meaning

32
00:01:20,219 --> 00:01:22,099
that you can be adding to your communication.

33
00:01:22,700 --> 00:01:24,920
This is often why a lot of people

34
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:26,859
misinterpret what other people are saying,

35
00:01:27,459 --> 00:01:30,959
why people miscommunicate and they misunderstand others.

36
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:33,579
It's simply because they're not adding enough context

37
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:35,159
to that communication.

38
00:01:36,079 --> 00:01:38,359
We need to learn to be more conscious

39
00:01:38,359 --> 00:01:39,579
of moving our face more.

40
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:41,840
And as you learn to become more conscious

41
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:44,299
