00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:56,980
at watching people's faces and you're

48
00:01:56,980 --> 00:01:59,260
able to listen with your eyes and not just your ears,

49
00:01:59,519 --> 00:02:01,780
you'll be able to understand people better.

50
00:02:02,140 --> 00:02:03,760
And if you learn how to use your face,

51
00:02:03,780 --> 00:02:05,859
and I know I'm really overdoing this message, but I really want

52
00:02:05,859 --> 00:02:07,780
to overdo it, and then if you get better

53
00:02:07,780 --> 00:02:10,319
at using your face to add more context,

54
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:13,099
this is how we create effective communication.

55
00:02:13,340 --> 00:02:14,740
This is a piece of the puzzle,

56
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:16,639
an important piece that's often missing.

57
00:02:17,520 --> 00:02:19,919
Now, as we go back to facial expressions,

58
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:23,099
