105
00:04:10,099 --> 00:04:11,599
When I first learned this,

106
00:04:11,659 --> 00:04:13,919
this was a very difficult area for me,

107
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:15,800
a very difficult area of body language

108
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:16,779
for me to get better at.

109
00:04:16,879 --> 00:04:20,100
Because in my culture, and especially during my upbringing,

110
00:04:20,339 --> 00:04:22,779
I was taught to kind of hide my feelings.

111
00:04:23,259 --> 00:04:26,060
In the Asian culture, you have this thing called thick face.

112
00:04:26,339 --> 00:04:27,899
There's even a book written about this,

113
00:04:27,980 --> 00:04:29,199
thick face, black heart.

114
00:04:29,379 --> 00:04:30,939
And the whole idea of it was,

115
00:04:31,019 --> 00:04:33,060
don't show other people what you're feeling.

116
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:34,620
Kind of hide those emotions

117
00:04:34,620 --> 00:04:37,439
by keeping a very thick and almost blank face.

118
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:41,279
And as a result of this being a pillar in my culture,

119
00:04:41,439 --> 00:04:44,540
I grew up not expressing much emotion with my face.

120
00:04:44,740 --> 00:04:47,259
And this worked against me for so many years

121
00:04:47,259 --> 00:04:48,720
because people will often say,

122
00:04:48,860 --> 00:04:50,920
how come you're not excited about this project?

123
00:04:51,259 --> 00:04:52,839
You're telling me you're excited,

124
00:04:52,899 --> 00:04:54,579
but I don't see that you're excited.

125
00:04:55,079 --> 00:04:57,600
And so I kept a lot of emotions on the inside

126
00:04:58,009 --> 00:05:00,740
and growing now as a leader in my own business

127
00:05:00,740 --> 00:05:02,160
and as a leader in my community,

128
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:03,759
and as a leader online,

129
00:05:04,319 --> 00:05:06,180
I've learned that it's so important

130
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:07,980
to show people how you're feeling,

131
00:05:08,120 --> 00:05:10,240
not just tell them how you're feeling.

132
00:05:10,439 --> 00:05:12,240
And it made me feel really uncomfortable

133
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:14,699
because when I first learned about facial expressions

134
00:05:14,699 --> 00:05:17,040
and being more expressive with my face,

135
00:05:17,120 --> 00:05:18,560
I felt like I was being a clown.

136
00:05:19,420 --> 00:05:21,319
I told my mentors, I said to them,

137
00:05:21,339 --> 00:05:23,279
I feel like I'm overdoing it.

138
00:05:23,319 --> 00:05:25,000
I feel like I'm being too much with my face.

139
00:05:25,519 --> 00:05:28,019
What I've learned over the years now as I look back is,

140
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:29,579
no, that's actually being effective.

141
00:05:29,740 --> 00:05:32,019
And the whole thing comes back into play when I said,

142
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:33,120
this is the universal laws.

143
00:05:33,500 --> 00:05:34,759
It's not that it's fake.

144
00:05:34,839 --> 00:05:35,879
It's not that it's phony.

145
00:05:35,980 --> 00:05:38,319
It's just that I was unfamiliar with it.

146
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:40,759
And anytime you do anything unfamiliar,

147
00:05:41,040 --> 00:05:44,000
it always feels like you're being a bit too much

148
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:45,480
or you're being a bit extra.

149
00:05:45,779 --> 00:05:48,939
What you have to understand is for more than 20 years,

150
00:05:49,220 --> 00:05:51,079
I didn't really use my face much.

151
00:05:51,240 --> 00:05:53,600
So I had a lot of muscles on my face

152
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:56,839
that I barely ever moved or that if I move them,

153
00:05:56,879 --> 00:05:57,899
I don't move them very well.

154
00:05:58,180 --> 00:06:00,639
So when I learned this from my theater coaches,

155
00:06:00,759 --> 00:06:01,720
they taught me a bunch

156
00:06:01,720 --> 00:06:04,860
of great exercises that I did them twice a day,

157
00:06:04,939 --> 00:06:06,420
sometimes three times a day,

158
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:08,459
just to try to loosen up some of those muscles

159
00:06:08,459 --> 00:06:10,800
and strengthen some of those facial muscles.

160
00:06:11,339 --> 00:06:12,620
You might find this helpful,

161
00:06:12,779 --> 00:06:15,079
especially if you find facial expressions difficult

162
00:06:15,079 --> 00:06:15,860
for you as well.

163
00:06:16,259 --> 00:06:19,480
Now, the first exercise was you've got to make your face

164
