if you start doing that at people.

195
00:08:01,660 --> 00:08:04,300
The powerful thing about learning facial expressions

196
00:08:04,300 --> 00:08:07,300
and learning how to use your body language more effectively

197
00:08:07,839 --> 00:08:10,379
is that the better you become at body language,

198
00:08:10,459 --> 00:08:11,779
the more aware you become

199
00:08:11,779 --> 00:08:13,319
of your body language,

200
00:08:13,540 --> 00:08:16,199
you get better at reading other people's body language.

201
00:08:16,420 --> 00:08:18,600
The final thing I'll say in this video is that

202
00:08:19,199 --> 00:08:21,620
your facial expressions can change the way

203
00:08:21,620 --> 00:08:22,540
that people see you.

204
00:08:22,660 --> 00:08:25,680
And it can change the way that people feel towards you.

205
00:08:25,720 --> 00:08:27,740
It can change the way that people treat you.

206
00:08:28,240 --> 00:08:31,040
Imagine I walk through my day with a default face

207
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:32,100
and a blank face.

208
00:08:32,679 --> 00:08:34,639
And whether I was talking to my colleagues,

209
00:08:34,779 --> 00:08:35,759
whether I was at lunch,

210
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:38,340
whether I was getting gas at the gas station,

211
00:08:38,480 --> 00:08:39,820
whether I was sitting on the bus,

212
00:08:39,840 --> 00:08:41,080
I always just had a blank face.

213
00:08:41,779 --> 00:08:43,159
Do you think the world would treat me differently

214
00:08:43,159 --> 00:08:44,480
if this was my default face?

215
00:08:45,159 --> 00:08:48,299
Yes, of course, I mean, people probably would be too afraid

216
00:08:48,299 --> 00:08:49,539
to come up to even talk to you

217
00:08:49,539 --> 00:08:50,860
if you had a blank face the whole time.

218
00:08:51,500 --> 00:08:53,500
Whereas how would the world treat you differently

219
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:55,779
if you walked around with a smile for most of the day?

220
00:08:56,100 --> 00:08:57,840
What happens if this was your default face?

221
00:08:58,320 --> 00:09:00,179
I mean, just from a logical point of view,

222
00:09:00,240 --> 00:09:01,720
we know this to be true, right?

223
00:09:01,919 --> 00:09:04,139
I mean, even in your brain, rationally,

224
00:09:04,159 --> 00:09:06,919
you understand that if you walk through life with a smile,

225
00:09:07,460 --> 00:09:08,860
the world's gonna treat you different.

226
00:09:09,019 --> 00:09:10,200
I mean, how cool is that?

227
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:11,759
That means we can use our facial expressions, right?

228
00:09:11,759 --> 00:09:17,179
expressions to change the way that other people feel about us. But also we can use our own facial

229
00:09:17,179 --> 00:09:22,480
expressions to change how we feel internally. We've learned now in psychology and understand

230
00:09:22,480 --> 00:09:27,840
that essentially you can use your emotions to lead your actions, meaning you could feel happy,

231
00:09:27,899 --> 00:09:34,379
then smile. But the opposite can also be true. You can smile and then feel happy. So the next

232
00:09:34,379 --> 00:09:39,460
time you feel down, if you just put on a slight smile, it will even help you feel a little better

233
00:09:39,460 --> 00:09:44,620
on the inside, let alone just how other people feel about you. And just remember that in the

234
00:09:44,620 --> 00:09:49,720
world of communication, if you are new to this, don't overwhelm yourself by trying to improve

235
00:09:49,720 --> 00:09:55,639
your facial expressions, improve your storytelling ability, and then improve your foundations. Don't

236
00:09:55,639 --> 00:10:00,340
try to do everything at once. If you struggle with facial expressions, I highly recommend that

237
00:10:00,340 --> 00:10:06,399
just focus on facial expressions that entire week. For the next whole week, all I'm going to focus on

238
00:10:06,399 --> 00:10:08,679
is being more expressive with my face.

239
00:10:08,899 --> 00:10:09,440
Remember,

240
00:10:09,460 --> 00:10:12,159
just take things one step at a time.

